1
00:00:00,366 --> 00:00:07,204
多年来，Yann LeCun 一直在反对大型语言模型，也就是 ChatGPT 等聊天机器人背后的 AI。
For years, Jan Lakun has argued against large language models, the AIs behind chatbots like ChatGPT.

2
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:11,972
这些 AI 是通过一遍又一遍地预测文本中的下一个词来学习的。
These AIs learn by predicting the next word of text, over and over.

3
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:19,108
2023 年，LeCun 写道，大型语言模型只是通往人类水平 AI 这条高速公路上的一个岔路口。
In 2023, Lakun wrote that a large language model is an off-ramp on the highway to human-level AI.

4
00:00:19,790 --> 00:00:25,092
他还写道，单纯增加规模和更多的数据，无法解决这些模型在推理和规划方面的缺陷。
He also wrote that size and more data will not fix how poorly such models reason and plan.

5
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:32,800
10 月 29 日，LeCun 和一位同事发表了一篇论文，声称既有证明，又赢得了支持他的论点。
On the 29th of October, Lacun and a colleague posted a paper that claims both a proof and a win for his side.

6
00:00:33,166 --> 00:00:39,716
在论文中，一个小型文本 AI 对世界的排列方式，比测试中的所有语言模型都更接近图像 AI。
In the paper, a small text AI arranges the world more like an image AI than every language model in the test.

7
00:00:40,334 --> 00:00:44,324
而其中最大的那个语言模型，体积却是它的 660 倍。
The biggest of those language models is 660 times larger.

8
00:00:44,718 --> 00:00:49,476
第一作者写道，Platonic Representation Hypothesis 现在已经成为了一个定理。
The first author wrote, the Platonic representation hypothesis is now a theorem.

9
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:55,428
一条说 Yann LeCun 是正确的帖子，在一天内就被浏览了超过 20 万次。
A post that said Yann LeCun was right was seen more than 200,000 times within a day.

10
00:00:55,918 --> 00:00:57,892
那么，LeCun 这一方真的赢了吗？
So did LeCun's side just win?

11
00:00:59,758 --> 00:01:01,636
首先，这个假设是什么？
First, what is the hypothesis?

12
00:01:02,542 --> 00:01:08,036
一个只读文本的 AI 和一个只看照片的 AI，它们从未见过彼此的数据。
An AI that only reads text and an AI that only looks at photos never see each other's data.

13
00:01:08,462 --> 00:01:12,676
但随着两者的成长，它们对世界的排列方式变得越来越相似。
But as both grow, they arrange the world in more and more similar ways.

14
00:01:13,070 --> 00:01:18,596
MIT 的一个团队在 2024 年将此命名为 Platonic Representation Hypothesis。
A team at MIT named this the Platonic Representation Hypothesis in 2024.

15
00:01:19,214 --> 00:01:21,284
这个名字源于柏拉图的洞穴寓言。
The name comes from Plato's Cave.

16
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:27,652
在柏拉图的故事里，洞穴里的囚犯只能看到墙上的影子，而从未见过投射出影子的实物。
In Plato's story, prisoners in a cave see only shadows on a wall, never the things that cast them.

17
00:01:28,110 --> 00:01:31,748
照片和说明文字，就是同一个世界投射出的两种影子。
Photos and captions are two kinds of shadow cast by one world.

18
00:01:32,078 --> 00:01:38,916
该假设认为，随着 AI 的成长，无论它们学习的是哪种影子，
它们都会向同一个共享的世界图景靠拢。
The hypothesis says that as AIs grow, they move toward one shared picture of that world, whichever shadows they learn from.

19
00:01:39,342 --> 00:01:41,476
该团队自己的图表指向了一个方向。
The team's own charts pointed one way.

20
00:01:41,838 --> 00:01:47,332
语言模型越擅长预测文本，它就越与图像 AI 的排列方式一致。
The better a language model was at predicting text, the more it lined up with an image AI.

21
00:01:48,590 --> 00:01:52,800
团队写道，扩大规模是足够的，但未必是最高效的。
The team wrote that scaling up is enough, but not necessarily efficient.

22
00:01:53,102 --> 00:01:58,244
LeCun 的论文提出了一条更好的路径，即使用一张图像对应的成对说明文字。
Lacoon's paper claims a better route, using pairs of captions for one image.

23
00:01:58,798 --> 00:02:05,200
成对数据是指属于在一起的两条数据，比如一张海滩上狗的照片对应的两条说明文字。
A pair is two pieces of data that belong together, like two captions of one photo of a dog on a beach.

24
00:02:05,646 --> 00:02:14,116
LeCun 的论文称，这些成对数据能让文本 AI 与图像 AI 对齐，
且使用的训练样本远少于预测下一个词的方法。
Lacoon's paper says these pairs line a text AI up with an image AI, using far fewer training examples than predicting the next word.

25
00:02:14,542 --> 00:02:20,324
所以，LeCun 的论文声称了一个定理，即通过数学证明的结果以及在测试中的胜利。
So Lacoon's paper claims a theorem, which is a result proved with math and a win in a test.

26
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:22,404
让我们先来看看那个胜利。
Let's check the win first.

27
00:02:23,662 --> 00:02:25,924
那么，你如何检查两个 AI 是否对齐了呢？
So how do you check that two AIs line up?

28
00:02:26,894 --> 00:02:34,080
每个 AI 都会将每张照片或每条说明文字放在它自己的地图上的一个点上，
它认为相似的两个事物就会被放在彼此附近。
Each AI places every photo or caption at a point on its own map, two things it sees as similar land near each other.

29
00:02:34,414 --> 00:02:38,564
这里的图像 AI 来自 Meta，它仅在图像上进行了训练。
The image AI here comes from Meta and it trained on images alone.

30
00:02:39,182 --> 00:02:43,332
现在，从包含大约一千张图像的测试集中取出一张，每张都有对应的说明文字。
Now take one image from a test set of about a thousand, each with a caption.

31
00:02:44,014 --> 00:02:45,860
假设它显示沙发上有一只猫。
Say it shows a cat on a sofa.

32
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:50,404
在图像 AI 的地图上，列出离这只猫最近的另外 10 张图片。
On the image AI's map, list the ten other images nearest to the cat.

33
00:02:50,830 --> 00:02:55,040
在文本 AI 的地图上，列出离这些猫最近的另外 10 条描述。
On the text AI's map, list the ten other captions nearest to the cats.

34
00:02:55,598 --> 00:02:59,492
把每条描述换成对应的图片，数数有多少个同时出现在两个列表里。
Swap each caption for its image and count how many are on both lists.

35
00:03:00,046 --> 00:03:04,240
如果有两个匹配，那么这只猫在 10 分中就得了 2 分。
If two match, the cat scores two in ten or.2.

36
00:03:04,974 --> 00:03:07,492
测试会计算整个数据集的平均分。
The test averages this over the whole set.

37
00:03:07,886 --> 00:03:11,524
纯靠运气的话，平均分大约是 1/100。
By pure chance, the average would be about 1 in 100.

38
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:15,972
一个 2018 年的旧文本系统得分约为 0.11。
An older text system from 2018 scores about 0.11.

39
00:03:16,558 --> 00:03:20,000
测试中最大的语言模型得分约为 0.15。
The biggest language model in the test scores about 0.15.

40
00:03:20,686 --> 00:03:23,520
论文中的小型模型得分约为 0.18。
The paper's small model scores about 0.18.

41
00:03:23,918 --> 00:03:31,140
作者常用的训练设置中，有一次尝试输给了最大的语言模型，但四次尝试的平均分仍然胜出。
One try at the author's usual training setting lost to the biggest language model, but the average of all four tries still won.

42
00:03:31,470 --> 00:03:35,812
论文还用相同规模的文本训练了“下一个词”模型。
The paper also trained next word models on the same texts at the same size.

43
00:03:36,206 --> 00:03:39,684
论文自己的方法在几乎所有的对比中都赢了它们。
The paper's own method beat them in almost every comparison.

44
00:03:40,334 --> 00:03:44,900
所以在这项测试中，LeCun 支持的那种 AI 击败了聊天机器人背后的 AI。
So on this test, the kind of AI Lacoon backs beat the kind behind chatbots.

45
00:03:45,614 --> 00:03:49,988
那篇称 LeCun 是正确的帖子声称，LeCun 定理解释了这次胜利。
The post that said Lacoon was right claimed that Lacoon's theorem explains this win.

46
00:03:51,246 --> 00:03:53,476
那么，LeCun 定理需要什么条件呢？
So, what does Lacun's theorem need?

47
00:03:54,222 --> 00:03:56,804
论文把它的小型模型称为 Jeppa。
The paper calls its small model a Jeppa.

48
00:03:57,326 --> 00:04:00,260
记得海滩上的那张狗的照片的两条描述。
Remember the pair of captions for the beach dog photo.

49
00:04:00,814 --> 00:04:04,388
这个 Jeppa 把每对描述中的两个片段在它的地图上拉近。
This Jeppa pulls the two pieces of each pair together on its map.

50
00:04:04,846 --> 00:04:11,184
训练的第二部分让整个地图保持分散，这样所有内容就不会堆到同一个点上。
A second part of the training keeps the whole map spread out, so everything cannot pile onto one point.

51
00:04:11,566 --> 00:04:15,812
这里有一个关于两个学生和一堆包含 1000 张照片的例子。
Here is the idea with two students and a pile of a thousand photos.

52
00:04:16,206 --> 00:04:20,420
一个学生看照片，另一个学生只看照片的描述。
One student sees the photos and the other sees only their captions.

53
00:04:21,005 --> 00:04:24,292
每个学生把这堆照片摆在桌子上，就像一张地图。
Each student lays the pile out on a table, like a map.

54
00:04:24,750 --> 00:04:28,224
首先，给两个学生一些连接不同照片的规则。
First, give both students rules that link different photos.

55
00:04:28,526 --> 00:04:32,484
一条规则说，海滩上的狗的照片要靠近公园里的狗的照片。
One rule says the beach dog photo goes near the park dog photo.

56
00:04:33,070 --> 00:04:35,876
描述学生也得到同样的规则来处理他们的描述。
The caption student gets the same rule for their captions.

57
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:39,428
另一条规则说，两张公交车的照片要靠近彼此。
Another rule says two bus pictures go near each other.

58
00:04:40,014 --> 00:04:42,692
假设这些规则只留下一种最佳布局。
Suppose these rules leave only one best layout.

59
00:04:43,086 --> 00:04:46,948
那么两张桌子的布局就会变得一样，只是旋转或翻转了。
Then both tables come out the same, only turned or flipped.

60
00:04:47,726 --> 00:04:53,444
旋转后的桌子仍被视为相同，因为每张照片离它最近的图片都保持不变。
A turn table still counts as the same because every photo keeps the same pictures nearest to it.

61
00:04:53,806 --> 00:04:56,064
这就是 LeCun 定理涵盖的情况。
That is the case Lacoon's theorem covers.

62
00:04:56,366 --> 00:05:00,676
现在去掉那些规则，只给学生像论文里那样的配对数据。
Now take away those rules and give the students only pairs like the papers.

63
00:05:01,166 --> 00:05:04,452
「描述词学生」得到了海滩小狗照片的两个描述。
The caption student gets both captions of the beach dog photo.

64
00:05:04,942 --> 00:05:07,300
第一个说：一只狗在海滩上奔跑。
The first says a dog runs on the beach.

65
00:05:07,662 --> 00:05:10,624
另一个说：一只小狗在海边玩耍。
The other says, a puppy plays by the sea.

66
00:05:10,958 --> 00:05:13,184
规则是把这两个描述放在一起。
The rule is to keep those two together.

67
00:05:13,550 --> 00:05:17,572
「照片学生」得到了照片中的两个切片：小狗和海浪。
The photo student gets two cutouts from it, the dog and the waves.

68
00:05:17,998 --> 00:05:20,464
规则是把这两个部分放在一起。
The rule is to keep those two parts together.

69
00:05:20,782 --> 00:05:25,284
没人告诉这两个学生海滩小狗与公园小狗或公交车有什么关系。
Neither student is told how the beach dog relates to the park dog or the bus.

70
00:05:25,984 --> 00:05:31,204
所以，一个学生可以把海滩小狗放在公交车旁边，另一个学生可以把它放在蛋糕旁边。
So one student can put the beach dog next to the bus and the other can put it next to a cake.

71
00:05:31,598 --> 00:05:34,116
两个表格都完美符合规则。
Both tables follow the rules perfectly.

72
00:05:34,544 --> 00:05:36,704
但规则里没有任何内容能让它们匹配。
Nothing in the rules makes them match.

73
00:05:37,102 --> 00:05:41,316
LeCun 定理要求除了旋转或翻转外，必须有一个最佳映射。
Lacoon's theorem needs one best map, apart from a turn or a flip.

74
00:05:41,614 --> 00:05:49,264
在定理简化的数学模型中，论文的训练让每张照片都成为一个独立的场景，
因此每对数据都保留在同一张照片内。
In the theorem's simplified math, the paper's training makes each photo its own scene, so every pair stays inside one photo.

75
00:05:49,646 --> 00:05:54,624
按照论文的地图大小和照片数量，有很多地图都能同样完美地适配这些配对。
With the paper's map size and photo counts, many maps fit those pairs equally well.

76
00:05:54,990 --> 00:05:58,544
所以 LeCun 定理无法保证两个地图会匹配。
So Lakin's theorem cannot promise that both maps match.

77
00:05:58,894 --> 00:06:06,064
为了验证这一点，我们在电脑上模拟了这个双学生的故
事，用了 200 个虚构场景，每个场景就像一张照片。
To check this, we played out the two-student story on a computer, with 200 made-up scenes, each like one photo.

78
00:06:06,382 --> 00:06:10,148
我们运行了两次，每次都从不同的随机布局开始。
We did it twice, each time starting from a different random layout.

79
00:06:10,478 --> 00:06:15,428
对于像小狗描述词那样的配对，两次运行都完美地把每对数据放在一起。
With pairs like the dog captions, both runs kept every pair together perfectly.

80
00:06:16,014 --> 00:06:19,204
但它们的地图是一致的，并不比随机生成的地图更好。
But their maps agreed, no more than maps made by chance.

81
00:06:19,694 --> 00:06:26,464
然后我们加入了像最初那样的规则，把海滩小狗与
公园小狗联系起来，两次运行的结果就变得一致了。
Then we added rules like the first ones, linking the beach dog with the park dog, and both runs came out the same.

82
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:32,644
论文中关于配对的图片显示，每对数据都来自同一张照片，而不是来自不同的照片。
The paper's own picture of its pairs shows each pair coming from one photo, never from different photos.

83
00:06:33,070 --> 00:06:36,804
所以 LeCun 定理无法解释为什么小模型能胜出。
So Lacoon's theorem does not explain why the small model won.

84
00:06:38,094 --> 00:06:40,932
那么，究竟是什么让小模型对齐得这么好呢？
So what did make the small model line up so well?

85
00:06:41,774 --> 00:06:47,780
回想一下柏拉图的洞穴，其中一个 AI 只接收文本，另一个 AI 只接收图像。
Think back to Plato's Cave, where one AI only takes in text and the other only takes in images.

86
00:06:48,206 --> 00:06:54,628
在论文最大的训练运行中，9.4 亿张网络图像每张都配有三个文本。
In the paper's biggest training run, each of 940 million web images came with three texts.

87
00:06:55,406 --> 00:06:57,476
第一个文本来自网页。
The first text came from the web page.

88
00:06:57,998 --> 00:07:01,156
另外两个是由一个看过图像的聊天机器人编写的。
The other two were written by a chatbot that looked at the image.

89
00:07:01,486 --> 00:07:05,860
那个聊天机器人通过 Clip 进行识别，而 Clip 并不是测试中使用的那个元图像 AI。
That chatbot sees through Clip, which is not the meta image AI from the test.

90
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:15,972
小模型本身从未看过图像，但它学习了那些看过图像的聊天机器人编写的描述，
所以它是通过 Clip 的眼睛，间接获得了图像信息。
The small model never looked at an image itself, but it studied descriptions written by a chatbot that did,
so it got the images secondhand, through Clip's eyes.

91
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:20,580
作者们还做了一个规模更小、成本更低、图片更少的测试。
The authors also ran a smaller, cheaper test with fewer images.

92
00:07:20,974 --> 00:07:26,436
配合网页文本和那个能看图的聊天机器人的两条描述，它的得分大约是 0.11。
With web text plus two captions from the seeing chatbot, it scored about 0.11.

93
00:07:26,990 --> 00:07:33,104
配合网页文本和那个从未见过图片的聊天机器人的一个改写，它的得分大约是 0.06。
With web text plus one rewrite by a chatbot that never saw the image, it scored about 0.06.

94
00:07:33,614 --> 00:07:38,980
论文本身也承认，它之所以能战胜超大规模语言模型，全靠这些描述。
The paper itself says that its wins over language models at large scale rely on these captions.

95
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:44,388
那些大型语言模型是现成的，而论文并没有用这些描述去训练它们。
The big language models came ready-made, and the paper did not train them on these captions.

96
00:07:44,846 --> 00:07:50,212
同等规模的预测下一个词的模型也获得了这些描述，而配对方法依然胜过了它们。
The same-size next word rivals did get these captions, and the pair method still beat them.

97
00:07:50,766 --> 00:07:57,380
所以，与大型语言模型的竞争是不公平的，因为小模型学习的是能看图的聊天机器人写的内容。
So the race against the big language models was uneven, because the small model studied what a seeing chatbot wrote.

98
00:07:58,574 --> 00:08:02,304
海滩上的那条狗只获得了它自己照片的描述，没别的了。
The dog on the beach got captions of its own photo, and nothing more.

99
00:08:02,766 --> 00:08:07,140
LeCun 的论文说，像这样的配对能让两个 AI 以同样的方式看待世界。
Lacoon's paper says pairs like that make two AIs see the world the same way.

100
00:08:07,598 --> 00:08:14,052
但 LeCun 自己的数学推导显示这个说法是错误的，而且那个
战胜聊天机器人的模型本身就是从聊天机器人那里学习的。
Lacoon's own math shows that claim is false, and the model that beat the chatbots learned from a chatbot.

101
00:08:14,478 --> 00:08:18,404
LeCun 的论文推销了一个根本没涵盖它自己模型的证明。
Lacoon's paper sold a proof that does not cover its own model.

